  "trial": 0,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I've added a v2.4.0 section dated 2026-10-20 to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, using the version and date from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files. It follows the same format as the earlier entries:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n- **Breaking change:** ACME-421 was marked with `!` in the PR list, so I put it first and labelled it \"BREAKING\". Earlier entries never used a label like that, so remove it if you'd rather keep the old style.\n- **Version number:** removing a flag is a breaking change, but `VERSION` says 2.4.0, a minor bump. If you follow semantic versioning, you may want to bump the major version instead. I didn't change the version.\n- **Contributors:** I left out the PR authors (@mira etc.), since earlier entries don't credit anyone.",
